# Penalty charge numbers

A TEC case has one **PCN stem** and one or more **penalty charge numbers**. A penalty charge
number is not a CCD case reference.

**PCN stem** is at the top of Case details, above State. It is also the case list column
(**PCN stem**) and the search filter (**Penalty charge number stem**). It identifies the case and
does not change when another registration is added.

**Penalty charge number** is the stem plus a one-digit suffix. Each registration has its own. The
Registration section on Case details shows the current registration: the highest suffix. Earlier
registrations are listed on **Previous registrations**, lowest suffix first. When the case has only
its current registration, that tab says **There are no previous registrations.**

A received form (TE9, TE7, PE3, or PE2) stores the full penalty charge number of the registration
that was current when the form was recorded. That can be an earlier suffix than the one shown in
Registration.

Technical detail, the authority-id map, and the seed scripts are on the tech docs site:
[Penalty charge numbers](http://localhost:4568/pcn-number.html).

## What the number looks like

```text
AA9999999X9
```

| Part | What it is | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `AA` | Local authority id, 2 or 3 letters. Part of the stem | `WE` for Westminster, `MC` for Manchester |
| `9999999` | Unique 7-digit number for that authority. Part of the stem | `2468037` |
| `X` | Check digit. Part of the stem | `8`, or `A` when the calculation leaves a remainder of 10 |
| `9` | Numeric suffix. Not part of the stem | `0` on the first registration; `1`, `2`, and so on for later ones |

The stem is everything except that final digit: `AA9999999X`.

A Westminster stem is 10 characters, for example `WE70599899`. Its penalty charge numbers are 11
characters, for example `WE705998990`. A 3-letter authority id makes a stem of 11 characters and a
penalty charge number of 12, for example `WCC123456700`.

The letters are the TEC authority id. They are not the FixedList code shown as **Local authority**
(`westminster`, `manchesterCityCouncil`). Seeded catalogue cases use Westminster, so their stems
and penalty charge numbers start with `WE`. File identifier and batch identifier on a registration
start with `RWE`.

The suffix marks another registration of the same charge. It is not part of the check digit. The
first registration is `0`. The next registration on that case is one higher, up to `9`.

## One case, several registrations

Stem `WE70599899`:

| Registration | Penalty charge number | Where it appears |
| --- | --- | --- |
| First | `WE705998990` | Previous registrations |
| Second | `WE705998991` | Previous registrations |
| Current | `WE705998992` | Case details, Registration |

